# Speed-to-Lead Config (EXAMPLE)

> This is an example config file. The real config is generated by Mode 0 (the 10-question setup interview) or hand-edited. Copy this file to `references/config.md` and replace **every** `[BRACKETED_PLACEHOLDER]` with your real values before drafting any leads.
>
> The example values below are illustrative only — they show the **shape** of a good config, not what yours should say.

Last updated: [YYYY-MM-DD]

## Lead sources
- Email ([YOUR_EMAIL@DOMAIN.COM])
- LinkedIn DM
- Website contact form ([YOUR_WEBSITE_URL])
- Referrals (any channel)
- [add or remove channels to match your reality]

## SLA target
- First response within: [5 / 15 / 60] minutes during business hours
- Outside business hours: [target, e.g. 2 hours / next business day]

## Primary CTA
- "[Your exact CTA copy, e.g. 'Book a 20-minute fit call']" → [YOUR_BOOKING_LINK]

## Routing rules
See `references/lead-routing-rules.md`

## Approved proof bank
- [Client/context]: [specific result or quote you have permission to share]
- [Client/context]: [specific result or quote — mark [anonymized] if name cannot be used]
- [Aggregate stat]: [e.g. "average X across last Y engagements"]
- [Public/social proof]: [e.g. audience size, awards, mentions — only if accurate and verifiable]

> Rule: if it's not in this list, the skill will not put it in a draft. If you want to add something, add it here first.

## Approved risk reversal
- "[Exact language you're willing to put in writing — e.g. 'Free 20-min fit call, no pitch']" — always OK
- "[Stronger guarantee, with conditions — e.g. 'If after the first 7 days you don't see a clear path to ROI, full refund']" — OK for [conditions, e.g. first-time clients only]
- Escalate to user for: [stronger guarantees, longer windows, custom terms]

## Pricing rules
- Mentionable without approval: [exact language — e.g. "engagements start at $X for a Y-day scope"]
- NOT mentionable without approval: [custom quotes, retainer pricing, enterprise pricing, etc.]
- Pre-approved discounts: [rule — e.g. "annual prepay = 10% off"; "referral from existing client = first month $0"; or "none"]

## Tone
- Descriptors: [3–5 adjectives — e.g. warm, direct, peer-level, dry humor OK, zero corporate filler]
- Opening examples:
  - "[Verbatim opener you would actually use #1]"
  - "[Verbatim opener you would actually use #2]"
  - "[Verbatim opener you would actually use #3]"
- Sign-off: [e.g. `- [First Name]`]
- Voice DON'Ts:
  - [e.g. No "Hope this finds you well"]
  - [e.g. No "Touch base" / "Circle back" / "Synergy"]
  - [e.g. No exclamation marks unless something is actually exciting]
  - [e.g. No emoji unless the inquiry used emoji]
  - [e.g. No hedging — direct or skip]

## Cadence
- Day 0: First response (within SLA)
- Day 1: Short bump
- Day 3: Proof/value share
- Day 7: No-oriented check-in
- Day 14: Close loop
- CTA strategy across sequence: [same primary CTA across all 5 touches / rotate per touch]

## CRM destination
- Where: [Local file / Notion database / Airtable / HubSpot / Pipedrive / Google Sheet / Gmail labels / other]
- Database ID or URL: [if applicable]
- MCP connected: [Yes/No — name the MCP if yes]
- Field mapping: [standard / list any non-standard mappings]

## Task destination
- Where: [Calendar reminders / Notion tasks / Asana / Things / manual / etc.]
- Auto-create after approval: [Yes if MCP connected / No]

## Owner
- Default owner for new leads: [Name / Role / Email]
- Routing exceptions: [e.g. "any lead from referral source X goes to [different owner]"]
